<section class="explanation" data-motion-section="sources" aria-labelledby="reader-explanation">
  <header>
    <h2 id="reader-explanation">A personal reader for the feeds you already follow.</h2>
    <p>Bring posts from ATProto and articles from RSS into one place. f.ads chooses a small selection for you to read together. That selection is an <strong>edition</strong>.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="source-map" aria-label="ATProto posts and RSS articles flow into your own f.ads reader">
    <div class="sources">
      <div class="source"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="24" cy="24" r="17"/><path d="M30 31c-2 2-8 3-11-1s-2-11 3-12 8 2 7 6-5 5-7 2 0-6 4-6m4-3v9c0 5 7 3 7-3"/></svg><div><h3>ATProto</h3><p>Your Bluesky<br/>home timeline</p></div></div>
      <div class="source"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="13" cy="35" r="3" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/><path d="M10 22a16 16 0 0 1 16 16M10 10a28 28 0 0 1 28 28"/></svg><div><h3>RSS</h3><p>Blogs and publications<br/>you subscribe to</p></div></div>
    </div>
    <svg class="connector" viewBox="0 0 120 220" aria-hidden="true"><path pathLength="1" d="M0 48H40Q60 48 60 68V152Q60 172 40 172H0M60 110H110m-12-10 12 10-12 10"/></svg>
    <svg class="mobile-connector" viewBox="0 0 40 64" aria-hidden="true"><path pathLength="1" d="M20 4V56m-10-12 10 12 10-12"/></svg>
    <div class="own-reader"><span class="reader-name">f.ads</span><p>Your own installation</p><div class="mini-edition"><span>Posts + articles</span><strong>One reading edition</strong><span>A beginning. A few pieces. An end.</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <p class="map-caption">Your sources supply the content. f.ads chooses the selection and puts it on a screen you control.</p>

  <div class="atproto-note"><h3>Already know ATProto?</h3><p>Sign in with your existing account. f.ads reads Bluesky posts through an AppView and keeps their original AT URIs. Your account stays with your existing host. Reading choices and feedback live in your f.ads installation; f.ads does not publish them as likes or posts.</p></div>
</section>

<section class="edition-explanation" data-motion-section="edition" aria-labelledby="edition-explanation">
  <header><h2 id="edition-explanation">From a busy feed to a manageable read.</h2><p>You decide what belongs in your reader, and how much room to leave for discovery.</p></header>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <div class="step-heading"><span>1</span><h3>Choose your sources and interests.</h3></div>
      <p>Add feeds and tell f.ads what interests you. You can mute a source whenever you want it out of your selections.</p>
      <svg class="step-art" viewBox="0 0 320 190" role="img" aria-labelledby="interests-title"><title id="interests-title">Example interests: design and science, with a source muted</title><rect x="15" y="22" width="180" height="43" rx="21" fill="oklch(0.887901 0.054623 275.009)"/><text x="38" y="50">+ Design</text><rect x="92" y="80" width="210" height="43" rx="21" fill="oklch(0.933164 0.133219 121.353)"/><text x="115" y="108">+ Science</text><rect x="25" y="138" width="228" height="38" rx="19" fill="none" stroke="oklch(0.628542 0.019740 275.462)"/><text x="46" y="164">− Muted source</text></svg>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="step-heading"><span>2</span><h3>Set the mood for this edition.</h3></div>
      <p>Curiosity leaves room for less familiar pieces. Energy helps match the selection to how much you feel like taking in.</p>
      <svg class="step-art" viewBox="0 0 320 190" role="img" aria-labelledby="mood-title"><title id="mood-title">Two independent controls: familiar to curious, and light reading to more depth</title><text x="12" y="32">Familiar</text><text x="308" y="32" text-anchor="end">Curious</text><path d="M15 60H305M15 149H305" stroke="oklch(0.784424 0.023047 274.657)" stroke-width="4"/><path pathLength="1" d="M15 60H220M15 149H100" stroke="oklch(0.489241 0.247585 267.098)" stroke-width="4"/><circle cx="220" cy="60" r="12" fill="oklch(0.489241 0.247585 267.098)"/><circle cx="100" cy="149" r="12" fill="oklch(0.489241 0.247585 267.098)"/><text x="12" y="122">Light reading</text><text x="308" y="122" text-anchor="end">More depth</text></svg>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="step-heading"><span>3</span><h3>Read an edition. Then stop.</h3></div>
      <p>Get up to twelve pieces, often fewer. See why a piece was selected, keep what matters, and reach a real end.</p>
      <svg class="step-art" viewBox="0 0 320 190" role="img" aria-labelledby="finite-title"><title id="finite-title">Three example pieces followed by an explicit end to the edition</title><rect x="12" y="14" width="296" height="31" rx="4" fill="oklch(0.887901 0.054623 275.009)"/><rect x="12" y="54" width="296" height="31" rx="4" fill="oklch(0.933164 0.133219 121.353)"/><rect x="12" y="94" width="296" height="31" rx="4" fill="oklch(0.870517 0.069476 29.532)"/><path d="M28 30H168M28 70H220M28 110H139" stroke="oklch(0.211881 0.024237 273.335)" stroke-width="3"/><path pathLength="1" d="m84 160 6 6 12-14" fill="none" stroke="oklch(0.489241 0.247585 267.098)" stroke-width="3"/><text x="113" y="167">Edition finished</text></svg>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="feedback-note"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path pathLength="1" d="M48 22A21 21 0 1 0 49 44M48 9v15H33"/></svg><div><h3>The next edition learns from what you tell it.</h3><p>Ask for more or less like a piece, or mark a good surprise. This feedback helps shape future selections. Your reading history and these choices stay in your own installation.</p></div></div>
</section>

